Scene summary: Hook: the quality coordinator stands at a whiteboard full of indicator numbers with many red circles; the team does not know which indicator to fix first. The product does not appear. 9:16 vertical, realistic live-action, shot on a modern smartphone | Primary Video Type: UGC Native (Rapat kecil tim mutu memilih prioritas perbaikan PKP) + Supporting Format: Product Demo | Handheld medium shots in a small puskesmas meeting corner with a whiteboard; one close-up of red circles on the board; Seq 3 single static tripod medium shot. REFERENCE PRIORITY: Use DNA Character as the authority for the talent's FACE and BODY identity only (not the outfit). Use DNA Product as the authority for the exact product identity. WARDROBE below overrides any outfit visible in the DNA Character image. CHARACTER LOCK: Use the DNA Character reference ONLY for the talent's face and body identity: exact face shape, jawline, skin tone, eye shape, eyebrows, hair or hijab style, body proportions and distinguishing features. Do NOT copy the outfit from the reference image; the outfit is defined in WARDROBE below. Keep the exact same face and body throughout the sequence. Do not add accessories or name tags not listed in WARDROBE. WARDROBE (OVERRIDES REFERENCE OUTFIT): Plain light green long-sleeve shirt with sleeves rolled to the forearm, dark gray trousers, black belt, simple silver watch. No lanyard, no name tag, no white coat. PRODUCT LOCK: Exact Kit PKP Puskesmas 2026 per Klaster ILP package from the DNA Product reference image (the real package mockup uploaded as an ingredient). Preserve the exact box colors, title text, cover design, proportions and visible design details exactly as in the reference. Do NOT invent a different box design. It may appear with a printed annual PKP report example in a clear folder, a printed management checklist, and a laptop showing the package's Excel tools (a colorful indicator recap with two charts, and a sheet listing the lowest indicators highlighted in red). Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the box. SET & PROPS: Small puskesmas meeting corner in the afternoon: a whiteboard covered with handwritten numbers and several red marker circles (no readable text), a table with printed indicator sheets and a laptop, two colleagues shown only as blurred shoulders, window daylight. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · close-up: his finger taps several red marker circles on the whiteboard (no readable text); cut to medium shot as he turns to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Indikator merahnya banyak sekali." Delivery (EN): tense, low voice 2–4s Problem · medium shot, he gestures at a stack of printed indicator sheets. VO (ID, verbatim): "Datanya tersebar di tiap klaster." Delivery (EN): honest 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, he looks at the blurred colleagues, then back to the lens. VO (ID, verbatim): "Tim bingung mulai dari mana." Delivery (EN): worried 6–8s Problem · medium shot, he holds two different printed sheets side by side. VO (ID, verbatim): "Rapatnya muter-muter terus." Delivery (EN): frustrated but calm 8–10s Beat · medium shot, he puts the marker down and exhales. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet room tone, marker squeak, papers shuffling. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent product details, claims, prices, ratings, testimonials, certifications, or guarantees. Keep exact talent face, the WARDROBE above, product shape, colors, packaging, box, printed report, laptop screen, laptop screen content, and visual details consistent with the DNA references.